<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see sun west, cloud east.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see sun west, cloud east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Wednesday were forecast to see sun in the west, cloud in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see mainly sunny skies with highs of 9 to 25 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see mainly sunny skies with highs of -1 to 17 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see mainly cloudy skies with highs of -5 to 10 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
